      "answer": {
        "text": "**State:** The proof strategy splits `thm:main` into three parts and assembles them: (i) the architecture-free contraction bound, and (ii-b) the outcome-credit bound, are both fully proved in Lean with no gaps — the outcome-credit proof literally combines the score-credit and zero-order-credit pieces (`Φ_out = Φ_score + Φ_0`) using the exponent comparisons `ε⁶λ^{n−3} ≤ ελ^n` and `ε²λ^{n−1} ≤ ελ^n`. The zero-order credit lemma (the `ζ=0` part of the Jacobian) is also fully proved, via a Lipschitz/frozen-ReLU argument.\n\n**What remains:** The one open piece is part (ii-a), the score-mediated credit bound (`Trace.Proof.unseenLettersScoreCredit` in `ScoreCredit.lean`) — this is the harder half of `lem:score-sum`, covering the higher-order ζ-Taylor terms, and is currently a placeholder with no proof yet. Everything else in the development builds on top of it rather than blocking it.\n\n**Author action:** None needed — this is the one remaining target and work on it is ongoing.",
